he logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Patients admitted to the ICU who are receiving vasoactive drugs.\n-  Age greater than or equal to 18 years old.\n-  Expected to remain admitted to the ICU for at least 24 hours post-enrolment.\n-  Clinicians who work in the intensive care unit where a patient participant has been admitted.\n-  An ICU clinician at the research site.\n-  Has used the ICU physical rehabilitation adverse event tool as part of this research study.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "AND": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "raw_text": "- Patients admitted to the ICU who are receiving vasoactive drugs.",\n                      "Eq-Comparison": [\n                        "receiving"\n                      ],\n                      "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n                        "receiving"\n                      ],\n                      "Encounter": [\n                        "admitted"\n                      ],\n                      "Location": [\n                        "ICU"\n                      ],\n                      "Drug": [\n                        "vasoactive drugs"\n                      ],\n                      "Drug-Name": [\n                        "vasoactive drugs"\n                      ]\n                    },\n                    "right": {\n                      "raw_text": "- Age greater than or equal to 18 years old.",\n                      "Eq-Comparison": [\n                        "greater than or equal to 18 years"\n                      ],\n                      