he logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n1. Preoperative patients have received relevant treatment, such as radiotherapy and chemotherapy;\n2. The subject has other diseases, such as tumors in other parts;\n3. Patients do not meet the age;\n4. There is no guarantee that other eating habits (such as eating fresh fruits and vegetables, not eating preserved foods) and other factors (such as BMI, smoking, drinking, etc.) are basically the same.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "OR": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "1. Preoperative patients have received relevant treatment, such as radiotherapy",\n                  "Procedure": [\n                    "radiotherapy",\n                    "operative",\n                    "treatment"\n                  ],\n                  "Procedure-Name": [\n                    "radiotherapy",\n                    "operative"\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Comparison": [\n                    "received"\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n                    "received"\n                  ]\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "raw_text": "and chemotherapy;",\n                  "Procedure": [\n                    "chemotherapy"\n                  ],\n                  "Procedure-Name": [\n                    "chemotherapy"\n                  ]\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            "right": {\n              "raw_text": "2. The subject has other diseases, such as tumors in other parts;",\n              "Condition": [\n                "dis