he logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  CES and non- CES diagnosis was according to Trial of Org 10172 in Acute Stroke Treatment ﴾TOAST﴿ classification criteria.\n-  non -CES were selected to match patients with CES regarding age and vascular risk factors as a control group.\n-  Patients with National Institutes of Health Stroke Scale ﴾NIHSS ﴿ score more than 5.\n-  Adult patients with their ages more than 18 year.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "- CES",\n                  "Condition": [\n                    "CES"\n                  ],\n                  "Condition-Name": [\n                    "CES"\n                  ]\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "NOT": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "raw_text": "and non- CES diagnosis was according to Trial of Org 10172 in Acute Stroke Treatment ﴾TOAST﴿ classification criteria.",\n                      "Condition": [\n                        "CES",\n                        "Stroke"\n                      ],\n                      "Condition-Name": [\n                        "CES",\n                        "Stroke"\n                      ],\n                      "Procedure": [\n                        "Trial of Org 10172 in Acute Stroke Treatment"\n                      ],\n                      "Procedure-Name": [\n                        "Trial of Org 10172 in Acute Stroke Treatment"\n                      ],\n                      "Negation": [\n                        "non"\n                      ]\n                